      "content": "For a work trip involving multiple cities, the Shinkansen is generally superior because it eliminates the time-consuming security lines and leg time associated with domestic flights. Traveling Tokyo to Osaka and Osaka to Fukuoka directly on the Shinkansen typically takes less total time than flying to/from the airport while accounting for airport transfers and screen queues. Given your priority on arriving on time for meetings without logistical stress, the high-speed rail network offers the most reliable and efficient connection.",
