      "content": "While low-cost carriers can sometimes offer ticket prices significantly lower than the Shinkansen, the total journey cost often remains comparable when including expensive airport transfers and baggage fees for flights. For a business traveler prioritizing schedule reliability and time efficiency, the extra expense of the train is usually justified rather than a significant financial burden. Booking a few weeks in advance might lock in a better price, but the Shinkansen remains the most predictable way to ensure you are in the meeting room exactly on time.",
